Z||000000||JohnF||11-12-2001||07:09 PM||||Due to my color blindness, the instrument lighting is just barely visible to me at night.<P>While I realize that the factory wanted lighting this color (looks dark orange & barely readable to me), can I change colors easily.  The "easily" comes from my thorough training to "keep it stock!".  <P>If changing is not too difficult, I could change back to factory original when necessary.  <P>If it's too difficult - I'll leave well enough alone!||||reg||5
Z||000001||Loki||11-12-2001||07:29 PM||||Pain in the ass   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">Not really, but the guage housing comes all apart.   It all depends, in my first Fiero i changed mine to green. Was ok and might have been brighter had I know about brighter bulbs. Basically depends on your set-up.On the back lit guages the light is reflected of a metal piece thats painted orange/red, which over time fades. If you get brighter bulbs and a paint thats HIGHLY reflective it would be easy to change the color to any color that can be had in reflective type......E-mail me with any questions....<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/fieroloki/lokisig1%20copy.jpg">  <BR>"All Fieros broke right now" :(||||reg||1
